Written once, applied repeatedly
On the left, one declared set held in a repository: value sets and profiles,
search parameters, which tenants a deployment serves, and whether a step is
automated. On the right, that same set applied as a run whose record is the
receipt — to a tenant being brought up for the first time, to one that has
been serving for two years, and to an appliance in a building. None of them
needed it rewritten.
